<title>USA: RockShox faces patent lawsuit.</title>
<headline>RockShox faces patent lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>RockShox Inc said it faces a patent infringement suit filed by Answer Products Inc.</p>
<p>The contested patent covers certain features of RockShox's current product line, Answer Products alleges in the suit.</p>
<p>Answer Products told RockShox it believes a settlement is the best resolution to this dispute, the company said.</p>
<p>RockShox, which manufactures suspension products for mountain bikes, said it also believes a settlement would best end the dispute. RockShox also said it plans to vigorously defend against the suit.</p>
<p>RockShox launched its initial public offering last week. The stock closed at 15-1/4, up 1/4 on Friday.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
